KG42.register("clusters-c83bae8fcfefc4a4fe59ad4c",{"id":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v142-d-K002","paper":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market","label":"Centralized welfare-maximizing clearing and accompanying nodal pricing","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-K002","label":"Centralized welfare-maximizing clearing and accompanying nodal pricing","market_meaning":"After all supply and demand bids have been received, the operator determines clearing quantities from the welfare objective and the applicable bid dependences, network constraints, and heat-quality constraints, recovers time-resolved, energy-carrier-resolved, and location-resolved prices compatible with the solution, and notifies the agents. The objective, feasible region, operational duties, and dual pricing together constitute a candidate mechanism; the mathematics and some applicability conditions are still not closed.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["LEM"],"process_stages":["clearing","coordination","pricing"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"Interpret within the model scope of linear, divisible bids. The special case of marginal bids with no network and no dependence, AND/OR dependence, network constraints, and the low-temperature DH example each retain their own conditions and are not generalized to one another. Financial independence of the operator is a preference; simultaneous clearing of energy carriers does not mean the same price. Currency, dimensions, and several price-compatibility conditions remain to be clarified.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"The welfare objective must share, with the clearing constraints, the clearing quantity of one and the same bid clearing, and the locational price is taken directly from the dual interface of the balance constraint of that optimization; the operator is responsible for reception, operation, and notification. The assembly basis is explicit information and decision dependence, not a shared operator node. The bid specification and the settlement applicability basis have their primary attribution elsewhere.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R003","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Bears the primary attribution of the clearing feasible region, dependence enforcement, network representation, and rolling results."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R004","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides the welfare objective of the same clearing, complementary to the constraint domain of R003, and is not counted separately as a duplicate clearing rule."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R005","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Bears the operational duties of centralized reception, continuous operation, the financial-independence preference, and result notification."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R007","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Recovers prices through the balance constraint of the same clearing, retaining the marginal-bid special case and the dependence and network conditions."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-L001","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C003"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C005","v141-c-R003::E::v141-c-R003-E007"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E022","v141-b-g01-E023","v141-b-g01-E040"],"rationale":"The source text explicitly states that the solution of the welfare optimization determines acceptance and rejection of bids; the objective chain provides the decision criterion for the clearing chain, and the two chains jointly describe one optimization."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-L002","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-x-y_b","v141-c-R004::theta::v141-c-R004-theta-q_b"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-X001","v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-T001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E002","v141-b-g01-E023","v141-b-g01-E024"],"rationale":"The clearing quantity in the objective and the clearing quantity in the constraints belong to the same bid outcome, and the bid quantity provides a common upper bound; the local roles of the variables and parameters of each chain are still retained separately."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-L003","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C001","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C002","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C005"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C006","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C007","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C008"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E006","v141-b-g01-E007"],"rationale":"The source text explicitly states that the center receives all bids, executes clearing, and notifies the results; demand reception and supply reception together constitute the condition that the full set of bids has arrived, and arrival of either side alone has not been interpreted as a sufficient condition."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-L004","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C015"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C007","v141-c-R007::x::v141-c-R007-x-lambda"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E036","v141-b-g01-E040","v141-b-g01-E041"],"rationale":"Balance constraint (12) and its period, energy-carrier, and location indices provide the dual interface for price recovery; λ is the price output and is not merged with the clearing quantity or the network quantity of the primal problem."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-L005","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C016","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C017","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C021","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C022"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C006","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C008","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C009"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E021","v141-b-g01-E025","v141-b-g01-E029","v141-b-g01-E043"],"rationale":"The network and AND/OR dependence change the interpretive scope of price compatibility; within-group compensation and location conditions are retained, and this is not used to prove per-bid profitability, or a necessary price difference, under every dependence combination."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-L006","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","kind":"alternative_representation","from_refs":["v141-c-R004::theta::v141-c-R004-theta-v_b"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R007::theta::v141-c-R007-theta-v"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E002","v141-b-g01-E015","v141-b-g01-E023","v141-b-g01-E042","v141-b-g02-E01"],"rationale":"The two records are used respectively for the objective coefficient and the marginal-bid valuation and point to the same class of bid attribute, but the currency transcription differs; only the unresolved statements of the associated parameters are linked, and the whole objective chain and the pricing chain are not treated as alternative rules."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-O001","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R004::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R005::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R007::V::bidding.demand"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R003::V::bidding.demand","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E007","v141-b-g01-E015","v141-b-g01-E022","v141-b-g01-E042"],"rationale":"All are occurrences of this mechanism's demand-bid submission node in the reception, optimization, and pricing chains; only the display citation is unified."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-O002","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::V::bidding.supply","v141-c-R004::V::bidding.supply","v141-c-R005::V::bidding.supply","v141-c-R007::V::bidding.supply"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R003::V::bidding.supply","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E007","v141-b-g01-E015","v141-b-g01-E022","v141-b-g01-E042"],"rationale":"All are the supply-bid submission node of the same mechanism; the related scientific clauses and edges are not deleted along with the representative citation."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-O003","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::V::clearing.local","v141-c-R007::V::clearing.local"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R003::V::clearing.local","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E022","v141-b-g01-E040"],"rationale":"The clearing on which pricing is based agrees with the local-optimization clearing described by R003."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-O004","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::V::clearing.social_welfare","v141-c-R004::V::clearing.social_welfare"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R004::V::clearing.social_welfare","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E022","v141-b-g01-E023"],"rationale":"Both refer to the welfare-objective node of that clearing, and the occurrence in the objective-specific chain is selected as the display representative."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-O005","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R005::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R007::V::coordination.local_operator"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R005::V::coordination.local_operator","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E006","v141-b-g01-E007","v141-b-g01-E040"],"rationale":"The source text assigns operating the clearing, reception and notification, and determining prices to the same market operator; software-agent or retailer roles are not merged on this basis."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-O006","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-X001","v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-x-y_b"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E002","v141-b-g01-E023","v141-b-g01-E024"],"rationale":"Both are the clearing quantity of each bid in the same optimization; the basis comes from an explicit definition and from the objective and upper-bound constraints, and not from the symbols being the same alone; the local roles in the feasible region and in the objective are retained separately."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-O007","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-T001","v141-c-R004::theta::v141-c-R004-theta-q_b"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E002","v141-b-g01-E024"],"rationale":"Both are the submitted quantity of the same bid and its clearing upper bound; the cross-chain association does not rewrite the parameter object or its binding."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-O008","kind":"alternative_representation","member_refs":["v141-c-R004::theta::v141-c-R004-theta-v_b","v141-c-R007::theta::v141-c-R007-theta-v"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E002","v141-b-g01-E015","v141-b-g01-E023","v141-b-g01-E042","v141-b-g02-E01"],"rationale":"The omitted index and the full index of the valuation can be associated through the source text, but the current currency records are not unified; alternative statements of parameters of the same class are retained, without selecting a representative, equating numerical values, or converting currencies."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G001","category":"unverified_source","description":"All assembly grounds still come from unaudited B candidate evidence, and the existing C2 bindings also do not mean that this experiment has completed an independent review.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003","v141-c-R004","v141-c-R005","v141-c-R007"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E002","v141-b-g01-E006","v141-b-g01-E007","v141-b-g01-E022","v141-b-g01-E023","v141-b-g01-E024","v141-b-g01-E036","v141-b-g01-E040","v141-b-g01-E041","v141-b-g01-E043"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually check the transcription, formula conditions, and pricing interpretation; at present only a semantic-assembly candidate awaiting inspection is formed."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G002","category":"math_incomplete","description":"The AND and OR expressions use the bid quantity as the denominator, but the frozen parameters do not give a strictly positive condition for these bids or a treatment of zero bid quantity; denominator validity cannot be supplied automatically from the upper-bound constraint.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003","v141-c-R004"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-T001","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C017","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C021","v141-c-R004::theta::v141-c-R004-theta-q_b"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E024","v141-b-g01-E025","v141-b-g01-E029"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"The upstream is to verify the allowable domain of bid quantities within a dependence and the treatment of zero values, and mathematical closure is to be judged only after the conditions have been supplied; D does not add parameter bounds."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G003","category":"math_incomplete","description":"Clearing quantity is labeled in kWh, and injection and outflow are labeled in kW, while (8) connects the two directly. A 1 h implementation can make the numerical values correspond, but the source text also allows other period lengths; the time conversion and the scale of the dual price of the balance constraint are not yet explicit.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003","v141-c-R004","v141-c-R007"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-X001","v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-X002","v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-X003","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C025","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C003","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C007"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E002","v141-b-g01-E012","v141-b-g01-E023","v141-b-g01-E032","v141-b-g01-E036","v141-b-g01-E041"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Verify the period convention for energy and power, the units of the objective and of the balance equation, and the shadow-price conversion scale; before supplementary evidence is provided, do not generalize to an arbitrary period length, and do not rewrite the frozen formulas."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G004","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"E002 and E015 are currently written as €/kWh, and E02-E01 is written as öre/kWh; the unit statement of R004 still says that the currency symbol is missing, whereas the R007 valuation is written as €/kWh. Numerical consistency of the valuation parameters and price units cannot be confirmed directly from the symbols or from a shared mechanism.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R004","v141-c-R007"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R004::theta::v141-c-R004-theta-v_b","v141-c-R007::theta::v141-c-R007-theta-v","v141-c-R007::x::v141-c-R007-x-lambda"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E002","v141-b-g01-E015","v141-b-g02-E01"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually verify the original currency text, and have the upstream make the valuation and price units explicit; this round retains the original fields and the unresolved alternative statements, and does not perform a conversion on its own."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G005","category":"math_incomplete","description":"Marginal bids, the acceptance/rejection sets under partial acceptance, tied bids, and price selection among multiple dual solutions still have no complete definition; profitability of a dependence as a whole and bid-price compatibility also lack verifiable formal conditions. The existing material is insufficient to prove that the stated compatible prices exist for both GE/EQ and overlapping dependences.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003","v141-c-R007"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C019","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C020","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C022","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C023","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C001","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C002","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C003","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C007","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C008"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E019","v141-b-g01-E027","v141-b-g01-E028","v141-b-g01-E030","v141-b-g01-E040","v141-b-g01-E041","v141-b-g01-E042","v141-b-g01-E043"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Supplement or make explicit the relevant sets, marginality, the dependence-payoff criterion, price selection, and the applicable dependence scope; the dual sign of the balance equality must also be made explicit and cannot take over the nonnegative domain from a generic inequality LP example."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G006","category":"scope_conflict","description":"R007-C009 states enforcement of network limits as locational prices being different, whereas R007-C006 takes congestion as the condition; the existence of a transmission limit cannot directly prove that a price difference must occur. The per-bid profitability narratives of E040 and E043 must also be distinguished from the dependence-wide compensation conditions of R003-C022 and R007-C008.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003","v141-c-R007"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C022","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C003","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C006","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C008","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C009"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E021","v141-b-g01-E040","v141-b-g01-E043"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually clarify whether the network constraints are in effect and the profitability interpretation of independent bids and of dependence combinations; retain the original clauses, and do not elevate a conditional statement to an unconditional guarantee."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G007","category":"ontology_extension","description":"Bid dependence, energy-carrier-specific pricing locations, and the low-temperature heat-source proportion constraint are still carried by a broad clearing node, and none of the related node proposals has been approved; these concepts cannot be treated as the same object merely because they all belong to clearing.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003","v141-c-R007"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C016","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C017","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C021","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C024","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C006"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E017","v141-b-g01-E021","v141-b-g01-E031","v141-b-g01-E037","v141-b-g01-E038","v141-b-g01-E039"],"proposal_ids":["proposal:bid-dependency","proposal:network-pricing-location","proposal:low-temperature-heat-constraint"],"required_work":"Manually assess the scope of the proposals relative to energy carriers, the network, and the DH example; this round cites only existing objects and does not add nodes or edges."}]},"rule_refs":["48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R003","48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R004","48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R005","48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R007"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-51f1ed6d657e2673","KG40-4a0e4a04a308d0b9","KG40-72006c4bf7355110","KG40-80b56ab23344a0b7","KG40-91eceef212419ef6"]});
